    "title": "Fort Wayne's slide continues with 5th loss in last 6 games - NewsBreak",
    "text": "SOUTH BEND, Ind. (WANE) – Padres 24th-ranked prospect & TinCaps starting pitcher Clark Candiotti gave up one earned run over three innings while striking out two, but it wasn’t enough as Fort Wayne fell to the Cubs 8-2 on Wednesday night in South Bend. Fort Wayne broke a 1-1 tie in the top of the fourth with an RBI single from Victor Duarte to score Rosman Verdugo. However, TinCaps reliever Fernando Sanchez gave up three earned runs in the bottom of the fifth as the Cubs took a 4-2 lead. Recently acquired C.J. Widger struggled in his TinCaps debut, giving up four earned runs in just 0.1 innings of work, as the Cubs broke the game open in the bottom of the seventh. The TinCaps have now lost 5 of their last 6 games, having been outscored 45-17 over that stretch. With Wednesday loss Fort Wayne falls to 49-54 overall and 18-20 in the second half of the Midwest League season. The Cubs and TinCaps play again at Four Winds Field on Thursday at 7:05 p.m. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
